  "tags": [
    "Array",
    "Math",
    "Matrix",
    "Simulation"
  ],
  "statement": "You are given an `m x n` integer matrix `mat` and an integer `k`. The matrix rows are 0-indexed.\n\nThe following process happens `k` times:\n\n*   **Even-indexed** rows (0, 2, 4, ...) are cyclically shifted to the left.\n\n![](./assets/matrix-similarity-after-cyclic-shifts-1.jpg)\n\n*   **Odd-indexed** rows (1, 3, 5, ...) are cyclically shifted to the right.\n\n![](./assets/matrix-similarity-after-cyclic-shifts-2.jpg)\n\nReturn `true` if the final modified matrix after `k` steps is identical to the original matrix, and `false` otherwise.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** mat = \\[\\[1,2,3\\],\\[4,5,6\\],\\[7,8,9\\]\\], k = 4\n\n**Output:** false\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nIn each step left shift is applied to rows 0 and 2 (even indices), and right shift to row 1 (odd index).\n\n![](./assets/matrix-similarity-after-cyclic-shifts-3.jpg)\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** mat = \\[\\[1,2,1,2\\],\\[5,5,5,5\\],\\[6,3,6,3\\]\\], k = 2\n\n**Output:** true\n\n**Explanation:**\n\n![](./assets/matrix-similarity-after-cyclic-shifts-4.jpg)\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n**Input:** mat = \\[\\[2,2\\],\\[2,2\\]\\], k = 3\n\n**Output:** true\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nAs all the values are equal in the matrix, even after performing cyclic shifts the matrix will remain the same.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n*   `1 <= mat.length <= 25`\n*   `1 <= mat[i].length <= 25`\n*   `1 <= mat[i][j] <= 25`\n*   `1 <= k <= 50`",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= mat.length <= 25",
    "1 <= mat[i].length <= 25",
    "1 <= mat[i][j] <= 25",
    "1 <= k <= 50"
  ],
